#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

char *protocol_base64_encode(const char *data, size_t len);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Encodes \f[CR]len\f[R] bytes of binary data pointed to by
\f[CR]data\f[R] into a NUL\-terminated base64 string using the standard
base64 alphabet (\f[CR]A\-Za\-z0\-9+/\f[R]) with \f[CR]=\f[R] padding.
.PP
The returned string is heap\-allocated with \f[CR]malloc(3)\f[R].
The caller is responsible for freeing it.
.PP
The output length is \f[CR]((len + 2) / 3) * 4\f[R] characters plus a
NUL terminator.
.PP
Base64 encoding is used throughout the bash\-server protocol to
transport binary\-safe payloads (command output, variable values,
function definitions) over the text\-based v1 protocol and in the
\f[CR]\(dqencoding\(dq:\(dqbase64\(dq\f[R] fields of v2 JSON messages.
